  "source": {
    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1713251,
          "username": "jhonmuller",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/ecccb3/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2025-12-06T06:11:43.755Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I’m getting ready to open a small Shopify store selling board games, card games, and a few accessories, and I’m realizing pretty quickly that managing all the different editions and versions is trickier than I expected. Some games have multiple expansions, limited releases, or updated printings, and I want everything to stay clear for customers without turning my catalog into a mess.</p>\n<p>For anyone who’s been down this road — how are you handling products with lots of variants? Do you keep everything under one main listing, or do you split certain versions into separate products? I’ve been looking at a couple of inventory/variant apps, but I’d love to hear what actually works in real day-to-day use instead of just what the app pages promise.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I found a thread on the Shopify Community: <a href=\"https://community.shopify.com/t/how-do-i-structure-a-lot-of-unique-variants-products/97282\">https://community.shopify.com/t/how-do-i-structure-a-lot-of-unique-variants-</a><a href=\"https://minecrraftapk.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">products</a> the original poster also faced this exact dilemma. They explore different approaches (all variants under one product, separate products for each unique version, hybrid approaches, etc.). I think their situation is pretty similar to what I expect for my store, so if you’ve followed that discussion or have similar experience, I’d really like to know what you’d recommend.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you run a game store or anything similar with collectible or edition-heavy products, I’d really appreciate your advice. How do you keep product pages clean and still make sure customers find the exact version they’re looking for? Any tips or lessons learned would be super helpful.</p>\n<p>Thanks in advance</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 2,
