      "id": 673127,
      "summarized_text": "The store owner is seeking a manageable way to organize board games, card games, and accessories with multiple printings, editions, and expansions while helping customers find the exact version they want. They ask whether to use variants within a single product listing, create separate listings, or combine both approaches, and whether inventory apps work well in practice.\n\nThe advice offered is to keep printings and options for the same game together as variants, making them easier to browse from one listing. Expansions and limited editions should be separate products linked from the main game page. This provides a suggested hybrid structure, but the discussion does not cover app recommendations or real-world implementation details, so those questions remain open.",
